# 🧠 Nova AI Companion — Analysis & Improvement Plan

## 1. What We Currently Have

### 1.1 Backend: [ai.service.ts](file:///D:/pfe/pfe%200.3/soullink-backend/src/modules/ai-companion/ai.service.ts)
| Feature | Current Implementation |
|---|---|
| **LLM Engine** | Groq API — `llama-3.3-70b-versatile` |
| **Context Window** | Last **20 messages** per call |
| **Long-term Memory** | Rolling **conversation summary** (regenerated every 30 messages, max 200 words) |
| **User Context Injected** | `displayName`, `bio`, `dateOfBirth`, Big Five scores, last 10 Soul Game responses, friend count |
| **Mood System (AI-side)** | Nova returns a `mood` field in JSON that drives avatar state |
| **Proactive Messaging** | ❌ Not implemented — Nova only replies, never initiates |
| **Emotion Detection** | Saved `emotionDetected` field on each DB message, but never used in logic |
| **Summary Trigger** | Every 30 messages (fire-and-forget, doesn't block response) |
| **Message Storage** | `AIConversation` (one per user) + `AIMessage` rows |

### 1.2 Frontend: [NovaContext.tsx](file:///D:/pfe/pfe%200.3/soullink-frontend/src/context/NovaContext.tsx)
| Feature | Current Implementation |
|---|---|
| **Mood States** | 20+ states: `neutral`, `happy`, `thinking`, `curious`, `sad`, `angry`, `angelic`, `blushed`, `bored`, `broken`, `crazy`, `cursed`, `surprised`, `laugh`, `disgusted`, `love`, `rich`, `melting`, `smart`, `egg` |
| **Keyword Detection** | Client-side regex on user messages: blush/happy/angry/angelic/smart triggers |
| **Inactivity Detection** | Sets mood to `bored` after 3 min no interaction or 5 min no chat |
| **Vengeance System** | 3-strike escalation when user insults Nova (chat lock, singularity) |
| **Message Cap** | Last **50 messages** kept in React state |
| **Visual Effects** | Storm, PacMan, Singularity, Heartbreak, Melting, Smart, Dancing, Egg |

### 1.3 How Smart Is Nova Currently?

**Score: 5/10** 🔶

**What it does well:**
- Has real personality with a detailed system prompt
- Injects Big Five + game choices into every call → knows the user psychologically
- Dynamic mood that influences tone (e.g., ALL CAPS when angry)
- Rolling summary prevents full amnesia in long conversations

**What it lacks:**
- No sense of **time** (doesn't know if it's morning, evening, or if 3 days passed)
- No **emotional continuity** — each session feels fresh even if the summary exists
- No **proactive initiative** — purely reactive
- No **friendship tracking** — doesn't know if user is a new acquaintance or an old friend
- No **user fact table** — facts are buried in the summary blob, can't be quickly retrieved
- Memory summary only updates every 30 messages and max 200 words — loses nuance fast

---

## 2. What to Improve

### 2.1 Memory Architecture — From Blob to Structured

**Current problem:** User facts (name, hobbies, struggles, goals) are embedded in a 200-word text blob. When Nova needs to recall "what game does this user play?", it has to rely on the LLM to find it inside a paragraph.

**Solution: Structured User Profile Table (`NovaUserMemory`)**

```sql
-- Proposed table: NovaUserMemory
model NovaUserMemory {
  id          String   @id @default(cuid())
  userId      String   @unique
  
  -- Fast-lookup structured fields
  nickname        String?       -- What user likes to be called
  occupation      String?       -- Job, student, etc.
  currentMood     String?       -- Last detected emotional state
  emotionalTrend  String?       -- "improving", "struggling", "stable"
  topInterests    String[]      -- ["music", "coding", "anime"]
  lifeGoals       String[]      -- ["become a dev", "make friends"]
  currentStruggles String[]     -- ["loneliness", "exam stress"]
  importantPeople  String[]     -- ["sister Sara", "friend Khalil"]
  lastTopicDiscussed String?    -- For conversation continuity
  insideJokes     String[]      -- Small references Nova can use
  preferredTone   String?       -- "casual", "deep", "playful"
  trustLevel      Int           @default(0)  -- 0-100 scale
  friendshipStage String        @default("NEW")  -- NEW → FAMILIAR → FRIEND → CLOSE → SOULMATE
  
  createdAt   DateTime @default(now())
  updatedAt   DateTime @updatedAt
  
  user User @relation(fields: [userId], references: [id])
}
```

**How to update it:** After every LLM response, run a **background extraction pass** that asks the LLM: *"From this conversation, extract/update any user facts in JSON format"* and upserts the table.

---

### 2.2 Memory Speed — Indexed Lookup Algorithm

Instead of injecting the full summary blob each time, build a **context builder** that picks only what's relevant:

```typescript
// Context Builder Algorithm
async function buildSmartContext(userId: string, userMessage: string): Promise<string> {
  const memory = await prisma.novaUserMemory.findUnique({ where: { userId } });
  const keywords = extractKeywords(userMessage); // simple tokenizer

  const contextParts: string[] = [];

  // Always include: identity + friendship stage
  contextParts.push(`User: ${memory.nickname || user.displayName}, Stage: ${memory.friendshipStage}`);
  contextParts.push(`Trust Level: ${memory.trustLevel}/100`);
  contextParts.push(`Emotional Trend: ${memory.emotionalTrend}`);

  // Conditional: only include if relevant to current message
  if (keywords.some(k => ["feel", "sad", "stress", "hard"].includes(k))) {
    contextParts.push(`Known struggles: ${memory.currentStruggles.join(", ")}`);
  }
  if (keywords.some(k => ["play", "game", "music", "hobby"].includes(k))) {
    contextParts.push(`Interests: ${memory.topInterests.join(", ")}`);
  }
  if (memory.insideJokes.length > 0) {
    contextParts.push(`Shared references: ${memory.insideJokes.join(", ")}`);
  }

  return contextParts.join("\n");
}
```

**Result:** Nova gets precise, relevant facts instantly — not a bag of words.

